# gate-goals — the evergreen goal rotation mesh-gate-evolve proposes from (one goal per line).
# Each goal describes a CALIBRATED PREDICATE the mesh could use as ledger data — small, natural-
# argument, boundary-testable. The generator names the gate itself; a name colliding with a
# committed row is REJECTED at the door (a generated row cannot shadow a committed one).
# Keep goals concrete: the admission harness demands boundary fixtures from BOTH sides.
battery percent band: 0 CHARGE below a low bound, 1 OK in band, 2 SHED above a high bound
disk-used percent alarm: 1 when used percent >= a critical bound, else 0, boundary exact
load average (x100) shed gate: 1 SHED when load >= a bound, else 0, like the load-gate reflex
temperature hysteresis: given temp and previous state (0|1), enter HOT at a high bound, leave only below a lower bound
stale-age gate: 1 STALE when age-seconds >= lease-seconds, else 0, lease passed as a param
retry backoff cap: given attempt count, answer min(base * attempt, cap) as the delay seconds
